# The bundled runtime's pinned versions — ONE place (docs/ops/bundled-runtime.md).
#
# `ops/release/build-runtime-deps.sh` sources this and refuses any tarball
# whose sha256 is not the one recorded here: a mirror that serves different
# bytes fails the build rather than shipping inside Metistry.app.
#
# Bumping a version means replacing BOTH lines. Get the new digest the way
# the script does — download it and `shasum -a 256` — and say in the PR why
# the version moved. NODE_VERSION must satisfy the root package.json's
# `engines.node`; a test asserts it.
#
# shellcheck disable=SC2034

# Node — the official darwin-arm64 build (nodejs.org/dist), cross-checked
# against that release's own SHASUMS256.txt as well as the pin below.
NODE_VERSION=22.23.2
NODE_SHA256=61130f394c1630d211dd50aecc4353d379480f36d3ac913cd85dbba1aed585c6

# PostgreSQL — built from source as a relocatable install. Major must equal
# PG_MAJOR in packages/cli/src/postgres.ts (docker-compose.yml pins pg17).
PG_VERSION=17.11
PG_SHA256=dd27f2b3c59e73ed14aa3324901242bf69a032a6347805f274e6260322d42979

# pgvector — compiled against the Postgres above via PG_CONFIG.
PGVECTOR_VERSION=0.8.6
PGVECTOR_SHA256=10bf9938906e5d643bbc4a7eea104b6f57ba4898e5b76b20e60484ea1d5a7f8f

# git — a minimal relocatable build (RUNTIME_PREFIX). A clean Mac has none
# until Xcode Command Line Tools are installed, and the reconciler spawns it.
#
# Held at 2.54.x deliberately: 2.55 introduced a Rust component
# (target/release/libgitcore.a) and its build needs cargo, which this script
# will not install and the macOS runner does not ship. Moving to 2.55+ means
# adding a Rust toolchain to the runtime-deps job first — a decision, not a
# version bump.
GIT_VERSION=2.54.0
GIT_SHA256=45e8107643a44e3ce46f5665beb35af3932fb0d70017687905ab5d4e3aafa8eb

# Sparkle CLI tools (generate_keys, sign_update, generate_appcast) —
# ops/release/fetch-sparkle-tools.sh downloads and verifies this pinned
# archive instead of the Homebrew cask, which is disabled (fails Gatekeeper,
# 2026-09-01). Bump: replace both lines with the new release's
# Sparkle-<ver>.tar.xz values (github.com/sparkle-project/Sparkle/releases),
# gotten by downloading it once and `shasum -a 256` — same as every other pin
# here.
SPARKLE_VERSION=2.9.6
SPARKLE_SHA256=52bf9e88cdd972fc0c81501377a880e90d47031bd8ca5462488f843e2609e192

# Sparkle EdDSA public key (safe to commit; the private key is in the owner Keychain + the SPARKLE_PRIVATE_KEY repo secret). Generated 2026-09-09.
SPARKLE_PUBLIC_ED_KEY=fWZAJ5y36RlH1xMgHFVyqh67igpS1BIp3w9UgLVCtQk=

# llama.cpp — the BUNDLED local model server (`runtime/llamacpp/bin/llama-server`),
# built from source with Metal on, exactly like Postgres and git: one signed
# binary, no third app to install (docs/research/2026-09-11-local-models-
# openrouter-opencode.md, addendum 2026-09-12). LM Studio and Ollama stay
# peers, discovered over /v1/models — this is only the no-install default.
#
# Upstream cuts semver releases (v0.4.1, 2026-09-14) alongside the nightly
# `b<number>` tags; pin a SEMVER one — a nightly is a build, not a version.
# Bump: replace both lines, and say in the PR which server behaviour moved.
LLAMACPP_VERSION=0.4.1
LLAMACPP_SHA256=ef3d5b1907a391500ae11b5e61a8e2022e0deaac9790899cad9c4e02f03bfb9a

# ---- provider tool packs (docs/ops/bundled-runtime.md, "Provider tool packs") ----
# Built by ops/release/build-remote-packs.sh into runtime/remote/<tool>/ and
# shipped as ONE RELEASE ASSET PER TOOL — never in the DMG, never in the
# runtime-deps pack. `metistry remote set <provider>` fetches a pack only
# when the owner picks that provider (plan §2.23, X-112). Same rule as every
# pin above: version + sha256, both lines replaced together, the reason in
# the PR.

# Tailscale — `tailscaled` + `tailscale` built from the pinned upstream tag's
# source archive (BSD-3; the LICENSE ships from the archive). The digest is
# of github.com/tailscale/tailscale/archive/refs/tags/v<version>.tar.gz. Its
# go.mod names the Go toolchain it needs (`go 1.27.1` at this tag); the build
# pins THAT toolchain (GOTOOLCHAIN below) rather than the runner image's go,
# and the go command fetches it verified against the Go checksum database.
# Bumping TAILSCALE_VERSION means re-reading the new tag's go.mod and moving
# TAILSCALE_GO_TOOLCHAIN with it.
TAILSCALE_VERSION=1.104.1
TAILSCALE_SHA256=bf868b2b1a46b9485d55bcda12c2d7573279ce4474bc6d607f42f1495db36ed8
TAILSCALE_GO_TOOLCHAIN=go1.27.1

# cloudflared — the official darwin-arm64 release binary (Apache-2.0),
# cross-checked against the digest GitHub publishes for that release asset
# and then RE-SIGNED under the Folded Space Labs identity: the upstream
# macOS binary is not reliably notarized (plan §2.23). Upstream tags are
# YYYY.M.N. The LICENSE is fetched from the repo at the same tag.
CLOUDFLARED_VERSION=2026.10.1
CLOUDFLARED_SHA256=647615df99d49cd179ea5e13ef760b9bbfb33630f6ae62f87e33dfadda60adcc
CLOUDFLARED_LICENSE_SHA256=58d1e17ffe5109a7ae296caafcadfdbe6a7d176f0bc4ab01e12a689b0499d8bd

# zrok — the zrok CLI's darwin_arm64 release tarball (Apache-2.0),
# cross-checked against the release's own checksums.sha256.txt and re-signed.
# v2 is the current line (zrok_<version>_darwin_arm64.tar.gz). The LICENSE
# is fetched from the repo at the same tag.
ZROK_VERSION=2.0.8
ZROK_SHA256=4bf2ec6cf7c42accdf96e575f7c163f0c4ab26ecb080b4ab481fc43ee1cdd98e
ZROK_LICENSE_SHA256=a1ac6968b53d0542a930420fc9933ee1ec3644bcf4278c77e8909c1876349dee
